From April 2025 to February 2026 I interned as a full-stack software developer at Amber Creative, a Singapore agency. I worked on platforms that real people use every day.

## Many platforms, many systems

In ten months I worked on ITE's Work-Study Diploma platform, the KiasuParents community site, Glovida-RX's prescriptions platform, and sites for IAL and IAL InLab.

Almost every one used a different mix of tools: Next.js and TypeScript on most, but also C# with Kentico, WordPress, Strapi, Storyblok and Directus as content editors, and GraphQL for data.

## Working in someone else's code

Client platforms already exist before you arrive. Most of my work was building new pages and features inside them, fixing bugs, and making sure a change in one place didn't break another.

## Why it matters

The internship is where I learned to ship to real users. It led straight into freelance work, and then into building StillGood.
